-- title:
--   Node pack at a supersingular place with no order-one j-difference
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ has characteristic $q$, and a level $N\ge 1$ with $q\nmid N$; fix modular polynomial data `data` of level $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi_q\equiv(C(X)^q-X)(C(X)-X^q)$ modulo $q$, and the integrality hypotheses $h\alpha,h\beta$ for the two degeneracy maps from full level $N$ to full level $Nq$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let `fm` be a fibre model of level $N$ over $A$ with reduction the residue map $A\to\kappa$, let `dataAll` assign modular polynomial data to every divisor of $N$, with the level-$N$ polynomial separable over $\kappa$ after reduction and passage to $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,\kappa$, let $P$ be a place specialization over these data whose specialization map `P.sp` is the one `fm.spPlace` attached to `fm`, and let $R$ be a prolongation tuple over $P$ satisfying the fixed-place order law `OrderLawFixed`. Let $w$ be a supersingular place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,N$ (rational, affine for the two generators, with $j$-value in the supersingular set for $q$), and assume that neither $w.\mathrm{ord}(j-j^{q^2})$ nor $w.\mathrm{ord}(j_N-j_N^{q^2})$ equals $1$, where $j=\mathrm{jqModC}\,\kappa$ and $j_N=\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\kappa\,N$. Then for every finite extension $K/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ there are a finite extension $K'\supseteq K$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, node coordinates $c$ of $R$ over $K'$ at $w$ (so $c.x$ has $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1$ zero and $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2$ of order $1$ at $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,q\,\kappa\,N\cdot w$, while $c.y$ has $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2$ zero and $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1$ of order $1$ at $w$), and an element $\varpi$ of the coefficient subring $A\cap K'$, such that $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ is a Noetherian local ring and: an element $d$ of $A\cap K'$ reduces to $0$ under the restricted residue map exactly when $\varpi\mid d$; the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ is generated by $R.\mathrm{nodeConst}\,K'\,w\,\varpi$, $c.x$ and $c.y$; every $g$ in that ring differs from the image of some constant $o\in A\cap K'$ by a non-unit; and for every such $g$, $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1(g)$ is zero or has non-negative order at $w$, and $\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2(g)$ is zero or has non-negative order at $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,q\,\kappa\,N\cdot w$.
--
--   This is the local analysis of a node on the fibre at $q$ of the modular curve of level $Nq$, in the case where neither of the two degeneracy coordinates has difference of order exactly one: it produces, after a finite enlargement of the field of constants, a presentation of the local ring at the node with maximal ideal generated by a uniformiser of the constants together with the two branch coordinates, plus the saturation and integrality properties of the two residues. It is used by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_commonUnit_pole_of_reduceFst_fixed_ordinary_residueField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_commonUnit_pole_of_reduceFst_fixed_ordinary_residueField), and complements the companion construction of node coordinates in the case where one of those orders equals one.
-- source:
